## Agents

<!-- agentsync:roles -->

Delegate by naming the agent: "spawn the `architect` agent to plan X", "have the `code-reviewer` review this diff". Codex has no agent picker and never delegates on its own, so this list is how it knows what to spawn. Codex loads agents (and skills) only once the project is **trusted**.

## Skills

- `grill-plan`: stress-test a plan before work starts (interactive or adversarial)
- `grill-converge`: harden a high-stakes plan with autonomous grill rounds plus one peer-CLI gate
- `orchestrate`: drive an approved plan through engineer → code-reviewer, one phase at a time
- `{{PROJECT_NAME}}-ground-truth`: project orientation (read this first)

Codex has no per-skill `/` entry: run `/skills` to list skills, or invoke one by name.

## Source of truth

Agents, skills, and rules live in `agents/`. Edit there, then run `bash agents/scripts/sync_agents.sh`. Never edit the generated `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.opencode/`, `.agents/`, `.github/agents/`, or this file directly.

